  "notes": {
    "raw": "\\*Data except enthalpy of formation at 298 K estimated. \nPhase change: 1235.08 K, melting point of Ag; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 2.700$ kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n298.15-2000 K: $Cp^{0} = 8.930 + 0.006 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.295 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$ \n$H^{0}-H_{298}^{0}=8.930\\times10^{-3}T+0.003\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+0.295\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-2.762$ \nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n298.15-1235.08 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hr}^{\\circ} = 78.835 - 0.513 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 1.075 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 17.550 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = 78.835 + 0.513 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 1.075 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 8.775 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} - 28.999 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \n1235.08-2000 K: $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = 78.122 - 3.241 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.157 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} - 4.650 T^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta \\mathrm{Gr}^{\\circ} = 78.122 + 3.241 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 0.157 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} - 2.325 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} - 46.700 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \nSource: Data from Mills (80) who estimated all except enthalpy of formation at 298 K. ",
    "lines_raw": [
      "\\*Data except enthalpy of formation at 298 K estimated.",
      "Phase change: 1235.08 K, melting point of Ag; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 2.700$ kcal/mol.",
